msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:171
msgid "Saves each page as a file and serves it to logged-out visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:198
msgid "Cache expiry (hours)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:200
msgid "How long a cached page is kept before xSpeed builds it again. 1 to 720 hours (30 days)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:231
msgid "Excluded URLs"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:232
msgid "Pages whose URL matches a line here are never cached. Plain text matches anywhere (/cart). A pattern with * matches from the start of the path: /cart/* matches /cart/items but not /shop/cart/items. ~ starts a regex."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:241
msgid "Excluded cookies"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:242
msgid "Visitors with a cookie whose name matches a line here always get a fresh page. One per line; * and ~regex work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:248
msgid "Excluded browsers and bots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:249
msgid "Visitors whose user agent contains a line here always get a fresh page. Useful for screenshot bots and uptime monitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:260
msgid "Ignored query parameters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:262
msgid "URL parameters to ignore, so /post?utm_source=x gets the same cached page as /post. Each line matches a whole parameter name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:267
msgid "Clear cache after updates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:268
msgid "Clear the page cache when a plugin, theme or WordPress is updated, so visitors never get old pages with broken asset links."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:273
msgid "Clear only the pages a change affects"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:274
msgid "When you publish, edit or delete a post, clear that post, the pages that list it and its feeds instead of the whole site. Pages with a post grid from a page builder, a block plugin or the theme are noted as they are built and cleared when the change can affect their list; turn this off if a grid still shows an old list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:275
msgid "Which pages are cleared"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:276
msgid "The post, its old address if it moved, the home page, the blog page, its categories, tags and author pages with every page of each, the date archives, feeds, the posts next to it, pages that show a Latest Posts or Query Loop block, directly or in a synced pattern, and pages noted running a post grid of their own (a page builder, block plugin, related-posts or theme list) that the change can affect. If your theme shows a list that can be on any page, and the change alters it, xSpeed clears the whole site instead: a Recent Posts, Archives or Calendar widget, a post list block, or a latest-posts grid from a page builder or plugin (usually a new post, or an edit to one of the newest few it shows), a page list or menu (a page published, withdrawn, renamed or moved), or a Categories or Tag Cloud list (a post moved to other categories or tags)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:281
msgid "Separate mobile cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:282
msgid "Keep a separate cached copy for phones. Turn on only if your theme or plugins show different pages on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:314
msgid "CDN or proxy in front"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:315
msgid "Tells your CDN or proxy not to store pages xSpeed does not cache. Leave on Detect automatically unless you know your provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:317
msgid "Cache in front of this site"
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/Cache/CacheModule.php:318
msgid "Naming your provider narrows the headers to the one it reads. Detect automatically works it out per request and otherwise sends a set every cache ignores unless it understands it, so it is safe not to know. Off stops the edge lifetime and cache tags. When an add-on that manages the edge, such as a Cloudflare Enterprise add-on, is active, the \"don't store\" headers for logged-in, cart and search pages still go out. Run \"wp xspeed cache edge\" to see what was detected and what gets sent."
msgstr ""

